---
import Card from "astro-theme-university/components/Card.astro";
import CardGrid from "astro-theme-university/components/CardGrid.astro";
import ContentLayout from "astro-theme-university/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import heroImage from "../assets/images/hero-home.avif";
import PriceChallenge from "../components/interactive/PriceChallenge.astro";
import { courseMeta } from "../course-config";
import { sessionLabels, siteConfig } from "../site-config";
---

<ContentLayout
  title={`${courseMeta.code}: ${courseMeta.title}`}
  description={courseMeta.description}
  heroImage={heroImage}
  heroImageAlt="A barcode-striped receipt background beside a price tag showing $249 struck through and $189, labelled Week 3 example"
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <ul class="course-tags" aria-label="Course tags">
    {courseMeta.tags.map((tag) => <li>{tag}</li>)}
  </ul>

  <p class="tagline">You calculate the price. The price calculates you.</p>

  <PriceChallenge />

  <h2>What you will do</h2>
  <p>
    Twelve weeks, one recurring purchase — a pair of $249 headphones — and one
    running argument: the sticker price is a starting point, not an answer.
    Each week adds a piece students learn to price properly: quantity,
    discounts, coupon rules, price history, context-dependent pricing,
    subscriptions, loyalty points, alternatives to buying new, the value of
    waiting, and the value of your own time. Three assessments ask students to
    apply this to a real promotion, a constrained shopping scenario, and
    finally a decision-support system they build and can explain.
  </p>

  <h2>Who it is for</h2>
  <p>
    Anyone who has stared at a "50% OFF" badge and wondered what number it's
    actually 50% of. No finance background is assumed — the mathematics stays
    at the level of percentages, averages and basic probability. What's
    assumed is a willingness to distrust a sticker price on purpose, and to
    show the working behind why.
  </p>

  <h2>Where to go next</h2>
  <CardGrid columns={2}>
    <Card title={sessionLabels.plural} href="/sessions/">
      <p>All twelve teaching weeks, in order, each building on the last.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="Assessment" href="/assessments/">
      <p>What is marked, what it is worth, and when it is due.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="Lectures" href="/lectures/">
      <p>Lecture outlines, including a full slide deck for Week 1.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="People" href="/people/">
      <p>Who teaches the course and how to reach them.</p>
    </Card>
  </CardGrid>
</ContentLayout>

<style>
  .course-tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-block: 0 1rem;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .course-tags li {
    padding: 0.25rem 0.65rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--at-text-secondary);
    background: var(--at-bg-alt);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .tagline {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--at-text-secondary);
    margin-block-end: 2rem;
  }
</style>
